        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(process): add starvation guard to priority command queue",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe command-lane priority queue can starve lower-priority work forever under a steady stream of same-or-higher-tier enqueues. Upstream already inserts by static priority; this PR adds time-based one-tier aging at drain time. A prior version promoted with plain `priority + 1`, so aged **default/normal** work (0 → 1) could tie fresh **foreground** and win by older enqueue time, which violates interactive-first scheduling.\n\nFixes #79589\n\n## Summary\n\n**Policy (foreground-preserving one-tier aging):**\n\n- After `STARVATION_PROMOTION_MS` (30s), entries may promote by at most one tier\n- Promotion is **capped strictly below the foreground tier** (`effective = min(priority + 1, foreground - 1)` for non-foreground work)\n- Background (-1) ages to normal (0); aged normal stays below fresh foreground (1)\n- Fresh user/foreground work always runs before aged normal and aged background\n- Aged background still beats fresh background\n\n**Files:**\n\n- `src/process/lanes.ts` — `STARVATION_PROMOTION_MS`\n- `src/process/command-queue.ts` — `effectivePriority` (capped), `pickNextIndex` drain selection\n- `src/process/command-queue.test.ts` — aged background, aged normal vs foreground, aged vs fresh background\n\n## Evidence\n\nLive production-module transcript on branch head: aged normal and aged background both lose to fresh foreground; aged background still wins over fresh background. Full capture under Real behavior proof.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Drain order must keep fresh foreground ahead of aged default-normal and aged background work, while still promoting aged background above fresh background after the starvation threshold.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS 26.5.2, Node from branch `feat/command-queue-priority` at `/tmp/oc-75299` after merge with current `upstream/main`, head after aging-cap fix.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n\n  Step 1. Merged current `upstream/main` into the branch and capped `effectivePriority` so aged normal cannot reach the foreground numeric tier.\n\n  Step 2. Ran a live (non-test-runner) script against production `enqueueCommandInLane` / `pickNextIndex` with a `Date.now` offset equal to `STARVATION_PROMOTION_MS + 1`:\n\n  ```bash\n  cd /tmp/oc-75299\n  pnpm exec tsx /tmp/proof-75299-live.mjs\n  ```\n\n- **Evidence after fix:** terminal output from the production modules:\n\n  ```console\n  $ pnpm exec tsx /tmp/proof-75299-live.mjs\n  === Live command-queue aging proof (production modules) ===\n  STARVATION_PROMOTION_MS = 30000\n  Date.now offset used to age entries without wall-clock wait\n\n  [aged-normal vs fresh-foreground] drain order: [ 'foreground', 'aged-normal' ]\n  [aged-background vs fresh-foreground] drain order: [ 'foreground', 'aged-background' ]\n  [aged-background vs fresh-background] drain order: [ 'aged-background', 'fresh-background' ]\n\n  ALL LIVE ORDERING CHECKS PASSED\n  ```\n\n  Cap in production source:\n\n  ```console\n  $ rg -n \"FOREGROUND_QUEUE_PRIORITY|Math.min\\(entry.priority\" src/process/command-queue.ts\n  311:const FOREGROUND_QUEUE_PRIORITY = 1;\n  324:  if (entry.priority >= FOREGROUND_QUEUE_PRIORITY) {\n  328:    return Math.min(entry.priority + 1, FOREGROUND_QUEUE_PRIORITY - 1);\n  ```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:** Fresh foreground always drains before aged normal and aged background. Aged background still drains before fresh background after the 30s promotion threshold. Aged normal can no longer promote into the foreground numeric tier (the prior `priority + 1` hole).\n- **What was not tested:** Multi-session live gateway under wall-clock multi-minute contention with real cron plus user traffic (this proof exercises the production queue module with the real drain path and promotion clock).\n",
        "branch": "feat/command-queue-priority",
